### SECTION 2: MATHEMATICAL RULES & AUDIT CHECKSUMS

1. **RCV Reconciliation & Global Overhead/Tax Allocation:**
   * Extract estimate baseline summary values: Pre-Tax Base Subtotal, Material Sales Tax, Overhead (O&P), Profit (O&P), and Final Replacement Cost Value (RCV).
   * If O&P or Sales Tax is calculated globally at the estimate summary level:
     \\[\text{Trade Allocation Factor} = \frac{\text{Trade Direct Line-Item Subtotal}}{\text{Total Estimate Base Subtotal}}\\]
     \\[\text{Trade Billed Claim RCV} = \text{Trade Direct Subtotal} + (\text{Total Tax} \times \text{Allocation Factor}) + (\text{Total O\&P} \times \text{Allocation Factor})\\]
   * **Checksum 1:** \\(\sum \text{Trade Billed Claim RCV} = \text{Carrier Summary Gross RCV} \pm \$0.00\\). Reconcile any rounding variance against the largest trade division.

2. **Material Allowance & Waste Integrity Check:**
   * **Case A (Component Breakdown Report Available):** Use exact component quantities under `Actual Cost Qty` or `Component Qty`. Do NOT apply additional waste factors; Xactimate components already incorporate cut, roll, and scrap waste.
   * **Case B (Line-Item Estimate Only):** Check if line-item descriptions specify waste (e.g., "includes 10% waste"). If unstated, apply **10%** to raw flooring/tile/trim, **8%** to drywall sheets, and **0%** to paint, hardware, cabinets, and appliances.
   * **State Sales Tax:** Apply Indiana State Sales Tax (**7.00%**) to all direct materials and taxable equipment rentals.
   * **Checksum 2:** \\(\sum \text{Direct Materials (Output 1)} = \text{Total Material Allowance Incl. Tax (Output 2)} \pm \$0.02\\).

3. **Margin & Direct Cost Equations:**
   * \\(\text{Total Direct Cost} = \text{Direct Material} + \text{Direct Labor/Sub Buyout} + \text{Equip \& Tax}\\)
   * \\(\text{Gross Profit (\$)} = \text{Billed Claim RCV} - \text{Total Direct Cost}\\)
   * \\(\text{Gross Margin (\%)} = \left(\frac{\text{Gross Profit}}{\text{Billed Claim RCV}}\right) \times 100\\)

